# object.m = value, and nobody knows the object. The stub that asks the site compares the structure, jumps through the table of handlers and stores: 22 instructions with the four at the site.
# In a loop the code asks the site itself: the structure, then that the record names a word of the object's own in its cell, then the store and the barrier: 11. Whatever else the record says, and every miss, is the stub's as before, and the stub alone fills the site.
# A store of a number goes by an address that the preheader finds: here nobody knows the value.
# function once(object, value) { object.m = value; }  function turns(object, n, value) { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) object.m = value; }  sink(once); sink(turns);
# OPTIONS: report=Flow mechanisms=all
# RUN: bytes-by-form Body
# CHECK-NOT: the build failed
# CHECK-NOT: PropSet Always Anywhere Open
# CHECK: PropSet Always Anywhere Closed 1 [[call]] [[call]]
# CHECK: PropSet Always Loop Open 1 [[inLine]] [[inLine]]
# CHECK-NOT: not named:
# The call of the stub stands outside rare code, so the report finds a call where the emitter says Open. Where shapes take turns at a site every other store goes on to the stub, and a call in rare code saves and restores round itself what the loop keeps in registers.
# CHECK: looks otherwise: PropSet Always Loop Open 1 found Open 0 Closed 1 Runtime 0
# CHECK: every form is named
# RUN(COUNT): compile SiteCachedStoresEmittedInline
# COUNT: statistic SiteCachedStoresEmittedInline 1
module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="sink" [isFreeName]
    v2 = NewClosure function=f1
    v3 = Call v1, -, v2
    v4 = NewClosure function=f2
    v5 = Call v1, -, v4
    Return v5
}
function f1 name="once" module=m0 length=2 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=anything}, {type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything, v1: anything):
    PropSet v0, v1 key="m" @20
    Return
}
function f2 name="turns" module=m0 length=3 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=anything}, {type=anything}, {type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything, v1: anything, v2: anything):
    v3 = Integer
    Jump -> next b1(v3)
  b1(v4):
    LoopHint
    v6 = Less v4, v1
    Branch v6 -> taken b2(), notTaken b3()
  b2():
    PropSet v0, v2 key="m" @40
    v8 = Increment v4
    Jump -> next b1(v8)
  b3():
    Return
}
